/* Model-owned refinements/root-handoff declarations; imported by shared-heap-smp.sysml. */
package GambitSharedHeapSmpRootHandoffRefinement {
 private import GambitSharedHeapSmp::*;

 part metadataPinExitHandoff:SourceCase {
  attribute :>> id="metadataPinExitHandoff";
  attribute :>> precondition="Exact VM incarnation, pinned source domain and activation generation identify one accepted transfer per activation; nested calls have separate existing activation records. Bound parent loan and target protection survive unlocked handoff. Source metadata is ordinary C data accessed under its one selected gate; route admission uses a qualified acquire/release backend. All count/generation increments are checked before mutation, with no wrap or timeout-based reset. Arbitrary asynchronous death inside a locked/allocator prefix is not admitted.";
  attribute :>> argument="Selected field layout extends existing holders, not a history table: rc_domain owns view_epoch/view_held and short source readers/admission; activation_record owns generation, accept_phase, readers, transfer key (VM/source identity, activation generation and installation revision UWORDs), phase enum, parent RC handle, durable target handle and cleanup reservation; The first local VM observer pin conservatively retains source route descriptors/domains/gates until source lookup and pin end; every source-destruction path honors it, otherwise the pre-source-lock window still dangles. It defers frees, not healthy GC. lifecycle owns a local observer WORD (bit0 final-close, +2 per pin, checked MAX_FIX bound) protecting source routes. Reuse existing ordered-word/CAS service; acquire-only CAS cannot publish final close or last-use release. Require qualified full/acq_rel RMW, acquire closed-zero observation and one nonblocking route-pin attempt before registry read ends; never overwrite count with a close store. Existing rc_header links/data/root_count remain canonical and immutable in extent while frozen. Each task binds its metadata owner before exposure. Under source gate freeze seals topology and admitted canonical slot extents, then claim publishes scanner ownership; lock-free traversal is legal only while view and scan custody survive. Retain FROZEN/joined source view until actual restored or known pre-copy refusal closure, independently of task DONE. Target gate seals complete installed payload and durable protection, releases; parent gate commits exact-key ACK plus counter-only loan discharge once, releases; target settlement follows separately. No two source gates nest. Entry admission closes first; matching accepted-key settlement remains until terminal; then final settlement closes, pins drain and exclusive cleanup executes outside the source gate before clean IDLE or free is published. ACKED remains queryable while the result consumer retains its accepted-key right, even after target settlement. Existing SETTLED phase additionally requires known result consumption or qualified abandonment/revocation of that query right; no extra history table or delivery flag is needed. Parent-loan ACK and target scope root cleanup are separate acquired duties even if RC handles alias; two successful borrows need two returns, and ACKED authorizes only the matching parent return. Preserve target borrow/refcount cleanup and never infer obligations from pointer equality.";
  attribute :>> conclusion="One frozen root-handoff adapter combines metadata exclusion, topology/node lifetime, once-only loan settlement and last-reader retirement. Gate unlock/lock supplies release/acquire only for qualified mutex backends; moving canonical slot writes require collector ownership and post-restore reload, not query permission. Lost responses outside completed critical sections can be queried; unknown partial physical writes keep source/target and cleanup custody. Pending ACK does not retain all obsolete task epochs.";
  attribute :>> missing="No implementation yet of the proposed holder fields or gate-held operations. ACK commit, target settlement and result-consumer closure are three facts: IDLE requires the latter, and a lost reply cannot retire its own query evidence. A stale retired key never authorizes replay or physical release. Cover alloc/register/release/return/unlink, setup/reopen/refuse/cleanup, all task validators and reset paths, marker prepare/abort/kill, terminal lifecycle_close_context and idle reacquisition together. Parent counter discharge must not call public return_rc_root under its gate. Route-to-local pin acquisition needs a teardown-compatible nonblocking checked handoff before registry reader ends. Generation exhaustion refuses reuse while retaining debt. Installed target lifetime must outlive original owner exit through current and next GC source membership. Fresh key lookup searches retained active/retiring records under the source gate after source lifetime admission, without dereferencing an unpinned caller address; O(A) lookup is charged unless an existing protected direct handle is proven. Produce selected-TU atomic/mutex and generated cohort evidence; source anchors and model projection are insufficient.";
  attribute :>> acceptance="One real-C R3/W2 campaign covers last native release during unlocked frozen traversal, known refusal/restored drain, route-close versus query pin, all-argument installed-ready with legitimate FAL, lost target/ACK/settlement returns after unlock, duplicate and stale ACK, final reader versus abort/terminal/IDLE reuse, generation/count exhaustion and unknown stop. Lose ACK after commit, finish target settlement, and attempt IDLE while the consumer still owns the key: refuse reuse until result consumption or qualified abandonment and reader drain. Independent ownership/slot oracle checks no missing root or duplicate decrement; preserve map multi-shot/wind and next full-GC scan. Record bounded production cuts, selected GCC/C23 backend, no-probe CPU/pause/peak and actual affected official consumers. No native execution occurred for this design.";
  attribute :>> formalBoundary="Reuse existing QNT ownership/phase/last-consumer histories and Lean slot/interval/count laws. This source argument establishes required C adapter premises and native controls; it neither defines a second state machine nor proves C23 ordering, arbitrary native progress or bounded unknown retention.";
  attribute :>> counterexample="Scan leases alone cannot prevent release_rc from unlinking saved next. A target receipt with owner-bound lifetime fails after ACK and owner exit. ACK state and loan decrement in separate observable critical sections permit duplicate release. Gate-held public return_rc_root deadlocks recursively. Checking generation after dereferencing an unpinned reused record is too late. Clearing pins on timeout or allowing generation wrap admits ABA. Holding registry read through a local blocking lock can obstruct teardown. Declaring interrupted multi-store commit atomic cannot recover an unknown physical writer.";
  ref part :>> clause=freezeFailure;
  ref part :>> entrySite=packetRcFrozenChainLease;
  ref part :>> exitSite=packetActivationObserverRetirement;
 }

 part gambitAmplificationDelivery:SourceCase {
  attribute :>> id="gambitAmplificationDelivery";
  attribute :>> precondition="One exact generated-code/runtime subject; shared Scheme identity, proper tail calls, multi-shot control and dynamic-wind remain observable. A complete generated checkpoint/root view and parent-root protection precede any allocating native registration. R member-root domains and W collector workers have separate rosters; each domain can supply multiple task kinds/shards. Full GC, census and original physical budget remain the control.";
  attribute :>> argument="Scheme owns logical frame liveness, allocation bounds, PointId and wind/effect semantics. Modern C owns target layout, atomic publication, physical intervals and lifecycle. Release-publish a complete frozen root view only after writer/native-data exclusion; an acquire claim grants scan/update authority without granting source reclamation. Unique forwarding winner retains payload, frontier and Tail responsibility until initialized work transfers to a counted custodian. Strong producer closure precedes weak work; weak slot repair, restored roots and context space precede release completion. Each shot acquires completion, reloads canonical slots and obtains fresh execution authority while observing the same shared cells. Unknown claim, stop or join retains scoped debt; an independent VM proceeds only if it has no unresolved shared moving-heap or global-service dependency.";
  attribute :>> conclusion="This is one replacement of implicit carrier-based safety by generated semantic facts and explicit root/work/restore authority. Current full-GC correctness can qualify independently of subsequent generational scan exclusion. Fewer repeated scans or captures are predictions until exact-source work counts and matched native cost show them.";
  attribute :>> missing="Complete emitted poll/frame/allocation branch coverage; native borrow and raw-writer admission; canonical frame/denv/reflection and serialized-frame slot adapter; three-outcome own-queue drain and committed-claim settlement; private/Tail and weak closure; physical copy/restore capacity and exit last-user proof. Current anchors and diagnostic overlays do not close these C refinements.";
  attribute :>> acceptance="One packet joins SH-CUT-S, SH-ALIAS-S, SH-BOUNDARY-S, SH-EXEC-N and SH-COST-N. Use actual map callback capture and two restores across full GC, shared mutation and wind observations, independent live-referent/missed-slot negative, generated allocation/native entry, R3 W2 non-worker root source, delayed publication/claim result, carrier exit, weak repair and restoration. Bind replay/shrink to actual C cuts. Preserve original budgets, census and heap; compare equal completed work with no-probe official tfib/gcbench plus observer-only diagnostic cohorts. Retain failures and historical/current source separation.";
  attribute :>> formalBoundary="No new QNT or Lean model. QNT owns admission, claim/phase/reentry/exit histories under existing fairness assumptions. Lean owns complete canonical slot maps, injective forwarding and physical interval/accounting laws. C refinement must establish each premise; ASCENT links exact subjects and propagates open dependencies, and LLM review supplies an authored argument rather than proof. This case depends only on root-adapter cases; alias/domain refinement and native/cost gates remain separately joined at the existing joint workstream.";
  attribute :>> counterexample="A callback keeps its referent live through an RC root but a captured frame slot is not repaired; a busy queue is mistaken for empty; a forwarding loser drops the winner's unfinished Tail; a local RootTask DONE resumes before weak repair; a second shot reuses an old raw pointer; an unknown join frees an arena still reachable by a helper. Each invalidates the complete delivery even if map values or one throughput test happen to pass.";
  ref part :>> clause=freezeValidation;
  ref part :>> entrySite=rootEpoch;
  ref part :>> exitSite=rootEnd;
 }
 part acceptedRoundSimulation:SourceCase {
  attribute :>> id="acceptedRoundSimulation";
  attribute :>> precondition="One accepted collection with decision=1, fixed VM/round epoch, all cooperative source views complete, no unqualified raw/native writer and admitted publication happens-before edges";
  attribute :>> argument="root_round_begin/freezes/publication set roster, joined_round, FROZEN, READY and scan_leases under exclusion; collection-round barriers publish the accepted decision. Use C control location plus source/task/work state, not round enum alone, to abstract close/park/issue/pin/begin. Task claim/scan/finish are internal steps while aggregate pending remains nonzero. Strong DRAINING precedes weak scan and restore, so abstract finish requires their real closure; source reopen and final collective reload correspond to reopen/restore only after that cut.";
  attribute :>> conclusion="The accepted cooperative route has a concrete state/action correspondence candidate; a rejected guard that changes no abstract observable is a stutter, not proof of completion";
  attribute :>> missing="No total weak-memory forward simulation: raw borrower activity lacks a complete park census; unknown publication/forwarding can terminate rather than recover; the existing local QNT step has no accepted transition for the real pre-copy refusal/unpin rollback, so that path is not silently simulated";
  attribute :>> acceptance="Check every real participant branch and barrier with selected C backend; preserve known-refusal and unknown-result histories as OPEN refinement duties; no source or native positive attestation from this argument";
  attribute :>> formalBoundary="Existing shared_heap_cut/rc_freeze_publication own temporal transitions. pending=1 is an aggregate debt predicate, not C queue length; restores<2 is bounded; compiler/C11-C23 memory-order and fair progress remain separate source premises";
  attribute :>> counterexample="Mapping ROOT_ROUND_DRAINING or one DONE task directly to QNT phase2 can release roots before weak work and restore. Equating d->borrows with Host.raw can falsely reject a parked lifetime loan or falsely admit a live raw reader.";
  ref part :>> clause=freezePublish;
  ref part :>> entrySite=rootEpoch;
  ref part :>> exitSite=rootEnd;
 }
 part preRegistrationLoan:SourceCase {
  attribute :>> id="preRegistrationLoan";
  attribute :>> precondition="Before raw Scheme input is decoded, a managed parent/source root and VM lifetime/data-access grant already cover it, or the entire prefix has an explicit noncollecting/nonreentrant moving-cut exclusion. The admission key or stable caller-owned result slot is known before fallible publication. A newly returned target pointer cannot retroactively protect its own input or recover its own lost first return.";
  attribute :>> argument="Selected managed-entry design: borrow the existing parent/source activation and its admitted data view before begin_sfun; retain that loan while allocating native metadata outside source gates. Preserve the permanent/no-argument shortcut under its code/VM lifetime grant. _ptree2 emits the raw Scheme argument stores before collecting conversions, but parameter positions need not form a prefix: a raw argument at position2 may precede converted position1. Commit one stable raw-entry-ready fact only after procedure and all generated raw stores succeed. Then marker allocation and conversion may collect, using canonical reloads. The initial setup thunk needs either proven immovability or managed source protection; startup already carries a launch root. No target pointer returned after fallible work can bootstrap its own input protection.";
  attribute :>> conclusion="The handoff is source protection -> initialized private span -> source-gated membership and per-cell install -> exact observation/ACK -> parked access and post-GC reload. Linked membership and payload equality never supply install evidence. A successful ACK retires only the matching loan; clearing the source slot, source record retirement and target last use require their own access/lifetime guards.";
  attribute :>> missing="Implement the parent-entry loan and stable admission/output capture in the existing activation/root services; add an initialized raw-entry commit fact independent of FAL and registration. Do not use a contiguous argument high-water index or the dead C stack's sfun_rooted array as a persistent receipt. All VOID/SCMOBJ/general generated variants share the same preparation/commit/abort obligations; the descriptor cohort must reject older unprotected generated entry before execution. A legacy protected prefix is admissible only with explicit freeze exclusion, not a second normal managed path. No GC/callback/cancellation occurs in the short metadata commit; arbitrary interrupted allocation/locked publication without actual stop/progress remains UNKNOWN.";
  attribute :>> acceptance="Use real SFUN variants and startup entry. Force closure/failure before registration, after empty link, after payload install, before ACK and after ACK before owner exit; verify a protected referent and each raw argument across GC. The target remains in a retained scan-visible domain through the next R3 W2 round even if the original owner exits. Unknown first admission keeps the parent/provisional target and cannot be retried blindly; asynchronous kill of an allocator/locked prefix is outside a safe takeover claim.";
  attribute :>> formalBoundary="Existing Host prepare/publish starts with managed root state; the pre-registration caller loan is a SOURCE PREMISE, not a proved transition of that kernel; no new QNT/Lean law is claimed";
  attribute :>> counterexample="Two source histories can have h->data=FAL and h->domain=d: registered empty node versus successful installation of legitimate Scheme FAL. Payload value or membership cannot distinguish them; no native failure is asserted";
  ref part :>> clause=freezeRoster;
  ref part :>> entrySite=foreignRootEmitter;
  ref part :>> exitSite=firstRootRegistration;
 }
 part parkReloadBorrow:SourceCase {
  attribute :>> id="parkReloadBorrow";
  attribute :>> precondition="Valid RC node/domain pin, registered source membership, all raw native accesses closed while GC mutates the slot, and acquire reentry after complete restoration";
  attribute :>> argument="borrow increments node/domain counters and returns &h->data; unlink requires both refcount and root_borrows zero. The header-data setter forbids changed borrowed procedure data; the new sfun_arg span writer instead requires the owning OPEN domain, no joined round and one accepted lifetime borrow. mark_rc scans both payload and span; call_sfun copies relocated span cells under the gate; marker reload occurs after make_vector and resize carries its cell through sync/GC before cleanup.";
  attribute :>> conclusion="The slot address can remain valid while its Scheme payload changes; under parked access and completed reentry a post-GC slot load can obtain the rewritten value; lifetime counters alone do not establish parking";
  attribute :>> missing="Complete active-read/write parking acknowledgment and reload coverage for every borrower, callback, allocating conversion and exceptional return; preserve exactly-one return and last-use retirement";
  attribute :>> acceptance="Audit resize/launch/marker/client call paths; native GC between borrow/use/reload plus nested escape and unknown result; never validate by comparing only pre-GC copied payloads";
  attribute :>> formalBoundary="Host park/relocate/reload and shared_heap_cut restore supply temporal premises; C slot identity, publication and each actual native reader remain source refinement";
  attribute :>> counterexample="A plain read through a const borrowed pointer concurrent with mark_array is not made safe by positive borrow counters; this is a source-premise omission, not a claimed admitted interleaving";
  ref part :>> clause=freezeAccess;
  ref part :>> entrySite=rcBorrow;
  ref part :>> exitSite=borrowReentry;
 }
 part stillStrongClosure:SourceCase {
  attribute :>> id="stillStrongClosure";
  attribute :>> precondition="Every external count/list/payload writer is stopped or admitted by the same epoch protocol before GC still selection; remaining strong/weak producers are accounted by their existing owners";
  attribute :>> argument="still_obj_refcount_inc/dec directly mutate header-body counts; setup_still_objs_to_scan selects nonzero-count objects into strong work and marks zero-count objects -1; scan_still_objs_to_scan later consumes that work outside the direct RootTask union";
  attribute :>> conclusion="Six direct root kinds cannot alone establish full strong-root producer closure; under closed count/list writers the observed selection has a coherent cut, and its queued scan work must finish before resume";
  attribute :>> missing="Prove all count/list/payload callers quiescent or implement one admitted count/write protocol and late-work custody; atomic count operations alone would not repair selection-versus-late-root races";
  attribute :>> acceptance="Audit conversion/addref/release/client cleanup and setup/sweep; control zero/nonzero selection, legal parent-root transfer and attempted late operations; actual admission must exclude unprotected raw-pointer resurrection";
  attribute :>> formalBoundary="Existing GW-S producer closure and generational source owners retain this obligation; the composition kernel uses abstract producer acknowledgment and does not prove concrete still closure";
  attribute :>> counterexample="A hypothetical late zero-to-nonzero update after zero selection without another admitted root shows the missing premise; it is NOT asserted reachable under valid cooperative/parent-root assumptions";
  ref part :>> clause=freezeRoster;
  ref part :>> entrySite=stillRootRefcounts;
  ref part :>> exitSite=stillRootProducer;
 }
 part originRecoveryQuery:SourceCase {
  attribute :>> id="originRecoveryQuery";
  attribute :>> precondition="Same VM/round/source identity remains pinned; scan tasks may be assigned to W workers independently of R source owners; observer holds no implicit scan or mutation authority";
  attribute :>> argument="root_round_publish assigns member i to worker i%W; completed requires executor==PSTATE and stored executor, while reopen validates the original owner. Selected observer design: each published task binds a stable metadata owner at construction. RC/member bank/stack/globals use that source's RC gate; VM/symkey and round terminal facts use the coordinator source gate. All task publish/claim/scan-state/finish readers and writers use the same discipline, releasing before traversal. Existing global-registry exclusion remains necessary; when both gates are required use global gate before source metadata and never invert it in observation. Query returns scalar observations tagged with source/epoch; a separately observed round fact is not mislabeled an atomic multi-record snapshot.";
  attribute :>> conclusion="Worker completion is a local scan observation; publisher recovery must independently identify origin/enrollment and assignment epoch, while whole-round resume and payload transfer use different receipts";
  attribute :>> missing="Add the source observer in root.h/root-tasks and source/control pin guards in RC/lifecycle cleanup. Caller supplies a prebound VM/source admission and output location; query acquires its bounded read pin before task lookup, snapshots under the published metadata owner and releases read access before return. Keep installation settlement in the retained activation/source record, not a history table. Old per-round detail may return stale/superseded after reuse; this cannot erase committed installation or grant resume. Brief query pins must not wait for scan/GC completion or become lifetime-long old-round pins. Plain non-RC task stores must join the same gate discipline; observer-only locking is insufficient. Reject pin overflow/wrap; failed consistent observation remains UNKNOWN. Actual physical stop is still required before recovering an interrupted pin/lock prefix.";
  attribute :>> acceptance="Use actual R3 W2: member2's task executor is member0, while member2 or an admitted metadata-only observer queries the same pinned origin without changing current PSTATE or scan authority. Cover READY/CLAIMED/SCANNING/DONE and all-round restoration separately, epoch/member reuse, lost install return, failed gate observation, delayed ACK, owner exit and query-pin versus cleanup. Query may change only its declared pin bookkeeping, never claim, scan, finish, release a loan or authorize resume; concurrent workers may independently advance.";
  attribute :>> formalBoundary="Existing source/scan/retirement QNT owners supply control laws; no new scheduler model or native counterexample is inferred from the arithmetic witness";
  attribute :>> counterexample="At actual R3 W2 assignment, member2 owned by C has executor A=member0. A call on C with executor C fails the stored-executor match, and executor A fails current-PSTATE, even at DONE. This source/arithmetic witness shows a distinct observer role is needed; weakening claim/finish permissions would let the observer execute work rather than merely inspect it. A stale raw source pointer cannot be made safe by checking its epoch after dereference.";
  ref part :>> clause=freezeFailure;
  ref part :>> entrySite=workerSourceAssignment;
  ref part :>> exitSite=workerCompletionQuery;
 }
 part rootHandoffReplayBinding:SourceCase {
  attribute :>> id="rootHandoffReplayBinding";
  attribute :>> precondition="The same exact-source full-GC subject supplies protected entry, pinned source-role observation and actual root/claim/reentry cuts. The trace declares R3 W2 and bounded control/log storage before freezing; the existing p1 destructive API population stays unchanged.";
  attribute :>> argument="Extend the owned root-task/map fixtures and existing Scheme replay/shrink envelope. Schedule actual C cut grants by operation identity, origin, epoch and actor role; record emitted cut observations rather than pretending a trace command executed a store. Maintain real map frames/denv and independent expected roots while the real collector runs. Hooks inside source locks or a collector phase only capture pre-reserved scalar metadata; they never call Scheme, allocate, join, wait on a participant or print. Freeze-gated writes use the tested service; unknown outcomes keep their custodian. Validate observations and replay the same failure signature only after a legal reentry or terminal child result.";
  attribute :>> conclusion="Existing real root API replay, fixture-state worker-stop controls and real full-GC map controls can coexist in one owned testing path with distinct scopes. A new joint result requires the actual C observations and same topology for every required history. Reusing a shrink helper is useful but cannot itself establish production-cut coverage.";
  attribute :>> missing="Implement one topology-aware live-frame case in the existing fixture/helper, preserving p1 defaults. Pre-reserve C control/log slots from the admitted trace bounds, freeze the expected operation/source/epoch/actor and require every commanded production hook to hit. Choose delays before gate acquisition or after release; inner critical hooks only append bounded scalar observations. No Scheme allocation/callback or participant wait is introduced inside frozen/locked code. Keep expected observations independent of implementation return, qualify hook omission/stale identity/missing root with negative controls, and require the same actual-cut signature under dependency-preserving shrink. Actual stop uses lifecycle admission, never async kill. No fixture-only mismatch or unrelated successful map upgrades coverage.";
  attribute :>> acceptance="Joint schedules cover pre-registration close, legal FAL installation, lost install return with source query and once-only ACK, query-pin versus owner cleanup, member2 observation before/after worker0 DONE, local-DONE before weak/restored completion, stale epoch rejection and the next no-new-write full-GC round after owner exit. Replay/shrink preserves fixed R3 W2, parent/target lifetimes, dependency-closed setup and the failure's source/operation identity. Invalid histories, precondition exit72, timeout, incomplete trace or changed actor/topology are not property mismatches. Keep the real 11-GC/two-restore/wind map oracle and official populations; later minor-only faults remain separately scoped.";
  attribute :>> formalBoundary="QNT owns protocol interleavings and failure histories; Lean owns slot/alias/accounting implications. This adapter only specifies how actual C observations establish those existing premises and how native PBT checks implementation properties. The oracle is independently maintained against specification semantics, not copied from the same implementation return. No new transition or data proof is introduced.";
  attribute :>> counterexample="A fixed p1 child that clears stack/bank roots cannot prove an R3 W2 live-frame history. A worker-stop fixture mismatch followed by a successful map run does not prove that mismatch occurred in GC. Shrinking away registration until exit72, dropping a trace event or silently switching to a worker actor cannot be accepted as a smaller source-query failure.";
  ref part :>> clause=freezeValidation;
  ref part :>> entrySite=packetReplayNativeScope;
  ref part :>> exitSite=workerCompletionQuery;
 }
}
